{
  "summary": "Catches `std::runtime_error` during wallet creation so that external signer setup failures are reported gracefully instead of aborting the GUI process. Cleans up newly created database files and directories when wallet creation fails so retrying with the same wallet name does not collide with leftover files.",
  "problem": "When external signer setup fails during wallet creation, an uncaught `std::runtime_error` crashes `bitcoin-qt` because the GUI worker thread lacks an exception handler, while RPC catches it only generically as error code -1. In both cases, partially created database files and directories remain on disk, causing subsequent creation attempts with the same wallet name to fail with 'Database already exists'.",
  "evidence": [
    "Author provides reproduction steps using a mock signer on regtest: 'terminate called after throwing an instance of std::runtime_error, the process aborts, and trezor_t/wallet.dat is left behind' (description).",
    "Author notes the unhandled exception was previously documented in bitcoin-core/gui#395 and mitigated in bitcoin-core/gui#396 without being fully handled in the wallet creation path (description)."
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
